:: Carter Hero Award Part 2 [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 10>>
The award ceremony is about what you would expect from something like that. It starts with the presenter, an overly flamboyant man in a blue suit and brightly dyed hair, comes out on stage and gives a nice introduction. He reminds you a bit of the drama teacher at Preston; the same over-the-top energy. He talks about the awards, what they mean, the sponsors of the event, and even cracks a few decent jokes before introducing the mayor of the city, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas King</span>. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Thank you <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Flickerman</span> for that… unique introduction.”</span> The mayor opens, a smile on his face that doesn’t quite reach his eyes, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It is my upmost pleasure as your mayor to present to you the first of what we hope will be a long-running tradition of The Opal City Charity Awards. Opal City has a long history with hosting award shows for television, film, athletics, and all sorts of other skillful and creative endeavors, but for too long the most important amongst us have gone unrecognized. Those of us that put the community first go above and beyond for the sake of others. Those being honored today personify the values that those raised in and who call this city home cherish more than anything. Selflessness, kindness, and the strength to put others before yourself. Each of our community groups from the schools to the community center to the various organizations headquartered here in the city have chosen someone that represent these values, and we honor them today for all that they do.”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I won’t ramble too much longer, since I know we have a long night ahead of us, but I would like to thank my brother-in-law, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair Constantine</span>, for being the head organizer for this event.”</span> He points out your headmaster in the crowd, who smiles well enough, <span style="Color: Yellow">but seems a bit annoyed despite the praise,</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Now there is a man who knows what it means to put others first. If he wasn’t the organizer, I’m sure he’d be taking home more than one award tonight.”</span> The crowd laughs, those nearby nodding along and smirking at your headmaster. Seems <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair</span> has quite the reputation for charity. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But enough speeches. Allow me to introduce the principal of Opal City High School to start us off”</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
        {
            Name: "Carter",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Formal",
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

And like that, the ceremony begins. You and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> watch along, though it gets a little hard to pay attention when you don’t know half of these people being honored and each and every one of them goes on a few minute long speech about their various projects and organizations goals. It gets a bit ranty near the end and you teasingly ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> if he is going to give a long, drawn-out speech about superheroes or Ultraman or something. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Haha, nah. I just want to thank my family and friends and stuff.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> replies, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I don’t really plan stuff like they do, I sorta just do things or help out when I can. Though hearing about all this cool stuff other people do is so cool! Though makes it a little weird that I’m the one receiving the big award. I’m just a kid who helps old ladies and cleans up the park.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> chuckles nervously as you glare at him, telling him not to sell himself too short. <br>
<br>
Eventually, about 45 minutes in, there is a knocking at the door and a woman’s voice calls out. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You two ready in there? You’re about to go on.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> looks at you nervously, all his confidence he had sitting in here vanishing once it was actually time to go on stage. <span style="Color: LightGreen">You give him one last reassuring pat on the back and double check his shoes and fly for him before walking out towards the side of the stage.</span> <br>
<br>

<<linkreplace"Continue">>
It is only as you are walking up to the staging area just out of view of the crowd that you realize a very important detail that you forgot. <span style="Color: LightCoral">You have to go on stage as well! You feel your heart racing, wondering just how many people are out there watching and what’ll happen when all their eyes are on you!</span> You had been so worried about calming <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s nerves down and getting him ready to receive the award that you forgot all about the fact that you are going to be presenting the award to him! <br>
<br>
You can feel yourself breathing heavily and starting to panic a little when you suddenly feel a hand on your shoulder. You turn to see <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, still looking nervous himself, giving you a reassuring smile. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“We got this. Just a little award, right?”</span> <span style="Color: LightGreen">You return <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s smile, taking a deep breath as you prepare yourself.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“And here to present our final award tonight is the man himself, Headmaster of Preston Middle School, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair Constantine</span>!”</span> Mayor King introduces him as the crowd claps and cheers. The energy has clearly decreased after the near hour of awards and speeches, but there is also a certain fervor from this being the final and biggest award of the night. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair</span> walks up with a smile, waving to the crowd and chuckling as one person whistles a little too enthusiastically. <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Alistair",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Everyday",
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’ll cut right to it, since I’m sure everyone here is getting tired.”</span> He begins, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“This final award isn’t any more important than the others, as everyone here has done important work to make this community and the world a better place. No, instead this final award means something different. It isn’t about being a good person or fundraising or anything like that. This award is about being Opal City’s very own hero, hence the name, The Hero Award. I’m sure many of us read comic books as kids so we know that being a hero isn’t about being strong or smart or even wearing a tight colorful costume.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair</span> pauses as a few people laugh, including <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“No, being a hero is about doing what is right and helping others, even when it’s hard. Even when you may not be the strongest or the smartest or even the most brave. Being a hero is about having everything telling you that a problem is too big or too complicated for you to handle yet giving it your best shot. Because if not you, then who? The person receiving this award today is not only Opal City’s own little hero, but an inspiration that even those with decades more experience like myself can learn from. And here to present this award, is this boy’s close friend and classmate. Someone who, in the short time he has known him, understands the impact and importance of someone like this. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name $Player.LastName</span>, please bring the award out here.”</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Frown",
                Blush: 2,
            },
        },
        {
            Name: "Carter",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Formal",
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

You jump as your name is said out loud, fully immersed in <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair</span>’s speech. You are quickly handed a small box with a velvet cloth over it and rush out onto the stage, <span style="Color: LightCoral">instantly feeling your heart tense and your butt pucker as you see the sheer size of the audience! It must be over a hundred people!</span> You smile nervously as you walk out, holding the hidden award so tightly and becoming all too aware of your own two feet as you walk up to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair</span> and turn to face the crowd, <span style="Color: Yellow">frozen and unsure of what to do as you look at <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair</span> for instructions.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Let’s see this award.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair</span> says as he removes the cloth from the box and pulling out a curved glass plaque with a fancy certificate inside. On it, is not only a nice illustration of a hero holding up a planet, but it is also embroidered with the name of the award along with <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s name in shinnying blue letters. It actually looks pretty cool! <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“And now <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name</span> will introduce us to the boy receiving this award, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name</span>?”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightCoral">You freeze, not at all realizing you had to actually speak or give some little speech! You look to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair</span> who, to his credit, gives you an apologetic look.</span> Seems he realized he forgot to mention this to you. He steps back, lowering the mic to your level as you stare out into the crowd nervously, <span style="Color: LightCoral">no doubt bright red as you try to think about what to say.</span> <br>
<br>
You see <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Father</span> and brothers in the crowd, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Noah</span> jumping up and waving at you with two hands when your eyes meet until <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Father</span> quickly sits him back down and lowers his hands. You see your teachers, no doubt here to support the school. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Randolph</span> gives you a confirming nod, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">De Leon</span> a reassuring thumbs up, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Cheng</span> blushes and looks away as your eyes meet, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Hart</span>, expectedly, is sleeping, but is shoved awake by a woman sitting next to you. You also see some of your friends and classmates, brought here due to their families being members of the community. <br>
<br>
Then you see <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s family… <span style="Color: Yellow">or two of them at least.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s father sits in a reserved section near the front row, <span style="Color: Yellow">an empty seat next to him.</span> He claps with the rest, but when your eyes meet, he looks away. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> sits next to him, smiling but gives you a look, knowing that in just a moment, <span style="Color: LightCoral"><span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> will walk out and see that his entire family isn’t there. Just two of them.</span> You want to warn <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, to prepare him, not wanting the moment of realization to be broadcast to everyone. <span style="Color: LightCoral">Your heart breaks for him; the one thing he wanted was for his family, his whole family, to see him get this award. Only half of his family showed up.</span> You look back towards <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, who is blushing from <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair</span>’s words. <span style="Color: Pink">He gives you an embarrassed smile and a thumbs up. He looks so happy.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: Yellow">Now you have to decide what <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> means to you?</span> <br>
<br>
<div id="choice">
    <<link "Carter is a hero<br>">>
    <<replace "#choice">>
        <span style="Color: LightGreen">You tell them that <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> is a hero.</span> He doesn’t help people for rewards or fame or even because it’s the right thing to do, it’s just who he is. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s first thought whenever he sees someone in need is how he can help them, even at his own expense and peril. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> would give the shirt off his back to help someone, and often unintentionally ends up giving his shorts instead. The crowd laughs as you look at <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, <span style="Color: Pink">who is blushing deeper and hides his face in his hands as your eyes meet.</span> <span style="Color: LightGreen">You end your speech by once again saying that <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter Kent</span> is a hero not only to this city, but to you.</span> <br>
        <br>
        <<include"Carter Hero Award Part 2 2">>
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
    <<link "Carter is your friend<br>">>
    <<replace "#choice">>
        <span style="Color: LightGreen">You tell them that <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> is your friend.</span> The town sees him as a hero and a boy who always helps out those in need, but you see past that. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> has been friendly to you since you first moved here. You tell them how he dragged you along to clean the park and invited you to swim in his pool and hang out when his parents are working. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> has only known you since the start of the school year, but treats you like a brother. <span style="Color: LightGreen">That’s just who <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> is, everyone he meets he treats like a close friend with kindness and care, but you are one of the lucky ones to get to really call <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter Kent</span> one of your closest and dearest friends.</span> <br>
        <br>
        <<include"Carter Hero Award Part 2 2">>
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
    <<link "Carter is just a kid<br>">>
    <<replace "#choice">>
        <span style="Color: LightGreen">You tell them that <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> never really considered himself as special or a hero, he’s just a person, like everyone else here.</span> He doesn’t have superpowers, he’s small, and not the strongest. He’s just a kid who, despite his normality, always goes above and beyond. It is just like <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair</span> said, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> is an example to everyone. He tries his best, even if he fails, and he doesn’t let failure get to him. But it’s because <span style="Color: LightGreen"><span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> doesn’t see himself as special that makes him special. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> doesn’t think he deserves this award, because he thinks what he does is just stuff. Stuff anyone can do, and maybe he’s right, but it is not IF <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> can do this that makes him special. It’s that he DOES do it. That’s the reason <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter Kent</span> is a hero.</span> <br>
        <br>
        <<include"Carter Hero Award Part 2 2">>
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
</div>
<</linkreplace>>

:: Carter Hero Award Part 2 2 [nobr]

/* Intro */
The crowd claps as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> walks on stage, <span style="Color: Pink">trying to look cool and collected despite obviously trying hard not to cry from your words. He looks embarrassed and overjoyed and nervous all wrapped in one.</span> The crowd continues to cheer as you hand him the award, smiling at your friend who always puts others first. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair</span> shakes his hand, the three of you pose for a picture, then <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> turns towards the crowd, stepping to the mic <span style="Color: Yellow">when he suddenly freezes.</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Frown",
            },
        },
        {
            Name: "Carter",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Formal",
                Mouth: "Frown",
                Blush: 1,
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightCoral">You see his face flicker, just for a moment, his eyes locked on where his family sits. Where only his father and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> sit. You see his lips quiver, his eye twitch, you can see the sadness bubbling up.</span> But he stands strong, taking a deep breath, pushing down his clear disappointment like its simple nervousness.<span style="Color: Yellow"> His father gives him a smile, but there is clear guilt behind it.</span> <span style="Color: LightGreen"><span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> claps louder than everyone else, cheering for his little brother with the energy of 10, no doubt trying to make up for those not here.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: Yellow">There is a pause. A pause that only lasts a few seconds, but feels like minutes. Then <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> speaks.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Tha- thank you for this award. I… don’t think I deserve it. I don’t do anything all that special.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> takes a deep breath before looking up and smiling. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But… I accept it. It means so much to me that people can be inspired by the little things I do. Little things may be small, but they can make a difference in a person’s day, even in their life! And if you do enough little things, they become big things and build up into great things!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> laughs nervously, the crowd laughing as well or cooing at how cute the shy small boy is. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But, before I go, I want to thank the people that help me every day. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name</span> is a great friend who is always there for me and looks out for me, even when I don’t look after myself. My teachers and friends at school teach me things every day, not just about math and stuff, but about life and being a good person. But most importantly, I want to thank my family. My dad is my hero. He helps the city not just by catching bad guys, but by being there when people need him. Plus, he’s always there to help me when I trip or mess up. And my mom…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> pauses, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“she makes sure everyone is informed and knows about what’s going on in the world. She is dedicated to the truth and how important being honest and informed is. She always does the best she can in everything she does. And my big brother <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span>, who is always looking out for me, even when I get myself into trouble. He’s always teaching me and helping me learn how to be the best person I can be.”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“And my twin brother, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>.”</span> There is another pause. <span style="Color: Yellow"><span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s dad glances down towards the empty seat. Even <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> looks away for a second. It is clear who the reason behind only half of his family showing up.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Even if our relationship is complicated sometimes, you’re the reason I am who I am. I wouldn’t trade you for the world.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> smiles, genuinely, as he looks down at his family, the disappointment shoved away. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Thank you all for believing in not only me, but everyone here. Let’s work together to build a better world for those who come after.”</span> <br>
<br>
[[Continue|Carter Hero Award Part 3]]